# Placedon backend — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` and `.env.local` are gitignored and MUST stay that
# way: this file is the only one that belongs in version control, and it must never
# contain a real value.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here has a default that reaches the network. Every module that could make an
# external call refuses to construct until it is configured explicitly, so an unset
# variable produces a clear refusal rather than a surprise request.

# ── Local model (Ollama) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# checker/ollama_runner.py has NO default host on purpose. Unset means the runner
# raises NotConfigured rather than quietly talking to localhost.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=gemma3:1b

# ── Hosted model (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed if LLM_PROVIDER is set to a hosted provider. The model is never in a
# decision path; it narrates and extracts, and the deterministic layer verifies it.
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# LLM_MODE=stub
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Licensed corporate data (MCA21 aggregator) ──────────────────────────────
# checker/mca_aggregator.py is licensed-access ONLY. There is no default endpoint and
# no scraping fallback, enforced by an AST check that rejects playwright/selenium/bs4/
# requests imports. Set these only from a signed contract with an MCA-sanctioned
# aggregator. Scraping MCA21 would forfeit the risk-reduction product this sells.
# MCA_AGG_BASE_URL=
# MCA_AGG_API_KEY=

# ── Retrieval and OCR candidates (D6) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Wired as CANDIDATES only (checker/router.py CANDIDATES); nothing on the answer path
# calls them until a bake-off wins. Missing key -> VoyageUnavailable /
# SarvamUnavailable, never a fallback. Keys are read from here by checker/env.py and
# never printed.
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=
# SARVAM_API_KEY=
#
# Sarvam trains on uploads by default (sarvam.ai/privacy-policy). Until this line reads
# exactly `confirmed`, checker/sarvam_model.py sends ONLY public files the repo holds
# under corpus/sources/ or corpus/testdocs/. Set it only after opting out of training
# in Sarvam's dashboard. It is read from this FILE, not from the shell environment.
# SARVAM_TRAINING_OPT_OUT=
